think The declared source of truth per session-logs.md is GLOW_PROFILE.bron, which is gitignored -- so the named authority is the one file no guard on a fresh clone can open.
think Chose the driver as the reading: .claude/settings.json is what Claude Code actually loads, and a description agrees with the thing it describes.
think Wrote tools/fixtures/declared_model.sh as the single reading, resolving its settings path from its own location so a scan that cd'd into a pen still reads the real tree.
think Gate reads presence of the current id rather than absence of every other, so session-logs.md keeps its true account of Fable 5, Opus 4.8, and Opus 4.6.
obs The first drift pattern claude-[a-z0-9-]* returned 71 files -- claude-code, .claude-state, launch-claude-season.rish. A model id is a family and a number; narrowed to claude-(opus|sonnet|haiku|fable)-[0-9] and it reads 1.
obs Two folded index shelves under session-logs/date/ read as drift, their basenames carrying a day rather than a full stamp. Widening the basename pattern would put this scan at odds with the resolver, repointer, and census (REDS %175), so the scan reads the directory instead.
obs Rows %199-%200 folded to archive as %201 carried the living pin past 24,576 bytes; the pin now reads 19,352 and the monotone spine is green at 201 with no gaps.
